We just happen to be currently studying Dante's _Inferno_ this quarter
in the English class I'm taking. Hell (at least the inner part of it)
is supposed to have 10 basic levels or rings, as it is shown in the
book, with the inhabitants being guilty of worse and worse sins the
farther down you go. Some on the net have said that hell is too long
and boring, so perhaps we could decrease the number of hell levels
from ~20 to 10. An alternate (or additional) idea would be to have the
up staircases all be in the same location, like in the upper left
corner of the maze (the way they are in Vlad's tower). This would cut
down on the boring time spent looking for that staircase in hell
(which sometimes happens to be under a boulder), while still requiring
time for the player to get to the corner allowing the wizard to come
back a few times.

