>	I second the motion for a new special level.

I third!

A few more comments/additions:

There should be lots of ghosts all throughout hell, representing the
dead souls.

Demons and ghosts in additional to @'s shouldn't be affected by
Elbereth (or maybe make them all not effected by rings of conflict
either to make it less powerful). I think it was pretty lame that the
game allowed me to levitate over an Elbereth and whack on and kill
Demogorgon, Orcus, Geryon, Dispater, et al without even getting hit
back once.

What about Charon (as mentioned in the fortune cookies)? Remember he's
the one who rowed souls (who had to pay him) across the river Styx to
the underworld. Perhaps when you first enter the Gates of Hell special
level, you are on a shore and have to #chat with Charon and give him a
large amount of gold ($10,000 or such) in order to get across a
section of water (perhaps a section of it would become land after you
pay, being similar to the drawbridge). The level should be
non-teleport and there should be something that prevents you from
being able to levitate across (something like sinks on the shore?). Or
better yet have Charon be *after* Cerebus, so that you can kill the
dog (barely surviving) and then find that you don't have enough to pay
to get across the Styx, when suddenly a pissed off Cerebus regenerates
and comes after you!

I happen to love shops, altars, and special levels of all kinds, and I
guess many others do too and want some more things to make the game
not necessarily longer but more interesting. What about the Sphynx as
mentioned in the fortune cookies? I think it would be great to have
yet another Stronghold like level (The Sphynx level, perhaps after the
Medusa but before the Castle) where you have to answer the Sphynx's
riddle or outwit her in some way in order to get past (or survive).

I like the idea of having more and special monsters that perhaps
require more thought and logic as opposed to an AC -30/+8 Stormbringer
to kill. Once you get your weapon and armor rustproof it's basically
just hack and slash after that. For instance, make the weapons that
kill certain types of monsters do *lots* more damage to them, or else
kill them outright, so that the player will want to keep around their
Longsword named Whatever-rist (I'm sure I'm not the only one that just
throws one of those away whenever my God gives it to me). For another
example, here are a few creative (yet intuitive) things that could be
done to make Elementals more than just things to hack and slash at:

1) If you throw a potion or water or zap a wand of cold at a fire
   Elemental, it should "put it out", killing it!
2) Zapping a wand of fire at a water Elemental should make it
   evaporate, killing it. Zapping a wand of cold at one should make
   it freeze, perhaps making it a statue or paralyzing it for many turns.
3) Zapping a wand of digging at an earth Elemental should kill it
   outright or else do it great damage.
4) If the player is dumb enough to zap a wand of fire at a fire Elemental
   (or throw a potion of water at a water Elemental), don't just make
   the Elemental resist the effects, but make it *divide*, perhaps more
   than once! Or perhaps doing the above actions could *tame* the Elemental?
   (Water Elementals should be like gremlins if they can find a pool of water.)
5) Perhaps zapping a wand of fire/cold/lightning at an air Elemental
   should polymorph it into a fire/ice/energy vortex?

